  "body": "## What changed\r\n\r\nTest-only change, in `crates/app/tests/first_traverse_posed.rs`. It pins the\r\n#3127 off-origin rotary refusal in the two cases that #3248 names.\r\n\r\n- Two work-turning rotaries: a new rig `TwoWorkAPivot` (A and B on the\r\n  table, A's stated `pivot`). One test reads the refusal by name\r\n  (\"work-turning rotary A\", \"pivot or offset\", \"off the WCS origin\",\r\n  \"cannot be judged\"). A second test is the control: a zero pivot reads\r\n  the sphere as before, `OpStatus::Ok` and no first-traverse verdict at\r\n  clearance 20.\r\n- A vertical rotary pivot: a new rig `VerticalCPivot` (a rotary named C on\r\n  the table, no stated axis, so its RS-274 line is vertical; B rides the\r\n  head). One test reads `OpStatus::Ok` with the pivot at 40 mm over the\r\n  origin and at zero, so the single-rotary branch ignores a vertical\r\n  line's pivot by design and the posed law drops out.\r\n\r\nTo carry the refusal, `laid_bar_on` now takes the rig and returns the\r\nrefusal as `Err`, the way `contour5d_on` does; `laid_bar_on_two_rotaries`\r\nkeeps the panicking wrapper for the existing happy-path test. The refusal\r\nsurfaces as an `Err` of `GenerateOperation::new`, so the helper maps it\r\ninstead of the panicking `generate` helper.\r\n\r\nNo production code changes.\r\n\r\n## How tested\r\n\r\nQuick gate, `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`: green. One step,\r\n`app suites: first_traverse_posed`, ok in 83 s. The whole suite runs\r\n(the fixtures changed outside the test functions). Pinning tests:\r\n\r\n- `one_of_two_work_turning_rotaries_off_the_wcs_origin_refuses_by_name`\r\n- `a_zero_pivot_on_two_work_turning_rotaries_reads_the_sphere_as_before`\r\n- `a_vertical_work_turning_rotary_with_a_stated_pivot_is_not_refused`\r\n\r\n## What was not exercised\r\n\r\nNo posted G-code, no simulation, and no heavy lane in the review sense: the heavy dry-run maps this diff to\n`app heavy: first_traverse_posed`, a lane that runs 0 tests (the file carries\nno ignored test), so the lane did not run. The vertical case asserts that generation succeeds and no first-traverse\r\nverdict appears; it does not assert the swept stock height, because the\r\nlaw drops out.\r\n\r\nChangelog: none\r\n\r\nEffort: high\r\n\r\nFork synced at v0.25.0\r\n\r\nFixes #3248\r\n\r\n",
